# Stoneway -- ruins processional road, 14x28 (buffer 680/1300). Build: python3 amap2.py stoneway.amap
#
# HOOK: an arrow-straight walled avenue, unlike any winding Johto route. It leads from a
#   ruined south gate through overgrown courts to a sealed temple mound. Four Unown steles
#   along the way spell the word that opens it. A cousin to the Ruins of Alph: same
#   chamber-mound grammar (6a/70/6b, 73 doors), plus gray fence walls (40-4a) as the stonework.
# BEATS (S to N):
#   1. South gate: rubble pillars (0a) flank the avenue. STELE_1 (47) stands in the grass.
#   2. Cloisters: two fenced garden boxes with tall grass inside, each entered through one
#      gap in its bottom fence. cloister_item (W), hidden_cloister (E).
#   3. Court B: the west court is tall grass (Medium, STELE_2). The east court has a
#      collapsed shrine (20/21 Burned Tower rubble over a 0a + 82 well). The puzzle reward
#      well_offering is a hidden item at the well, set by the solve.
#   4. Broken stair: ledge rows (56) cross both side courts, a one-way drop from Court A to
#      Court B. The walled avenue (44/46, 2 cells wide) is the two-way spine, with gaps
#      into each court. A Psychic patrols it.
#   5. Court A: the west Ruin Annex mound (73, a small chamber, annex_item) and the east grass
#      (PokeManiac, STELE_3).
#   6. Temple plaza: a walled plaza with two guardian stones (0a) and STELE_4a/4b flanking
#      the SealedChamber door. A Researcher NPC explains the steles. A Sage covers the plaza.
#      PUZZLE_SEAL (an object, modelled as a boulder) blocks the door until the word is
#      spoken. The north exit leaves from the plaza's west gap.
# PUZZLE: steles 1-3 each show one Unown glyph (bg_events, the Unown font from the Ruins
#   puzzle), read in walking order. 4a/4b: "Speak the road's word" lets you pick from
#   letters. Correct: setevent, the seal object vanishes, and the well offering appears.
#   Inside the Sealed Chamber: an Unown-themed reward or encounter. It can count toward the
#   Alph shrine gate (26 Unown) as flavour, but must not replace it.
# REACHABILITY: N<->S on foot, no HMs. Only the Sealed Chamber is gated (by the puzzle).
# PLACEMENT: S = Route 32's north-west edge, by the Ruins gate (that may need a short gate
#   house, since Route 32's west side is forest). N = toward Route 36 / the Ruins north
#   chambers. ref RuinsOfAlphOutside.
# GAPS: the gray fences (40-4a) are Moomoo-farm fences reused as low walls. They read as
#   stone at a glance, but a real ruined wall or pillar block would sell it more. 20/21
#   rubble works well on its own.
ref RuinsOfAlphOutside
key m=71 y=68 z=69 Y=6a 7=70 9=6b c=6c k=72 d=6d e=6e f=6f
key q=40 w=41 v=42 l=44 j=46 b=48 n=49 x=4a W=82 R=20 U=21 s=45 S=47
